course: dictionary
lesson: 7963
title: One word, three meanings: recess
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and recess is one of them. The words around it are the context, and they show you which meaning the writer means. Read the sentence first, then choose.
explain: In school, recess is the break between lessons when children play outside. «At recess kids his age seem loud and silly» tells you Jules is in a playground, not a parliament or a wall. In the UK the same break is called "break" or "playtime", so the word you hear can depend on where you live.
explain: Recess can also mean a time when a parliament, court or other group stops working for a while. It can also mean a small space set back into a wall, like an alcove, where shelves might fit. Ask yourself: is this a school, a government, or a wall? The sentence will tell you.
fact: Recess means the break between lessons when children play outside, in the USA, Canada and Australia.
fact: In the UK, the same break is called "break" or "playtime".
fact: Recess can mean a time when a parliament, court or other group stops working for a while.
fact: Recess can mean a small space set back into a wall, like an alcove.
fact: Useful phrases: at recess, during recess, recess duty (when teachers watch over the playground), in recess.
exercise: In Montreal, «at recess kids his age seem loud and silly.» What does recess mean here? | A time when a court stops working | *The break between lessons when children play outside | A dinner for grown-ups | A small space set back into a wall
exercise: «At recess a kid brags about the Bears game.» Darnell goes quiet. What does recess mean here? | A time when parliament stops working | A school trip | An alcove with shelves | *The break between lessons when children play outside
exercise: «The books sat on shelves in the recess beside the fireplace.» What does recess mean here? | The break between lessons | A dinner at school | *A small space set back into a wall, like an alcove | A time when a court stops working
test: The parliament goes into recess for the summer. What does recess mean? | A snack at break | A small space in a wall | *Stops working for a while | Playtime in the school yard
test: In the UK, what would most children call recess? | *Break | Alcove | Recess duty | Parliament
exam: In «The court is in recess until Monday», what does recess mean? | A small space set back into a wall | *A time when the court stops working for a while | The break between lessons when children play outside | A snack eaten at school
